{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794757839,"nonce":"xNmTi/QrmDXe0iay+LNGiLNQbpQ=","message":"The unthreaded hand-written fixture's trap under fibers was Ash's: its direct wasm backend pushed a library native's arguments before the slot check, so the fiber transform refused every function calling a library native and gave it guards that trap while unwinding (Ash git-bug e88b1a0). Fixed in Ash's working tree; with it, run.sh wasm and gen-wasm pass with '[fiber] instrumented ... refused 0 ... 0 trap(s)'. ASH_FIBER_REPORT=1 on ash --build prints that report, the quick check for this class of problem.","files":null}]}